	• [ ] 0.4 CONFIRM — gateway-key match. Run PRE-3. Need gateways showing surfaces=2 (both pitboss + cmd-audit tag the same host). Gates the Bleed 4 join.
	• [ ] 0.5 CONFIRM — SSL/DTLS events ingest. Run PRE-4. NEW. Decides whether the quiet-88772 detector (H5) is runnable in Splunk or becomes an operator ask. /var/log/messages (NSPPE termination) is NOT in standard ns.log forwarding — note which half you have.
	• [ ] 0.6 CONFIRM — web access/error log ingest. Run PRE-5. NEW. Decides whether the webshell-interaction hunt (S3) and header hunt (H6) are runnable.
Phase 1 — Run the confirmed-surface searches (delivery + IOCs + infra)
	• [ ] 1.1 ACTION — Baseline delivery sweep. Run S1. Record counts by wave; flag any unparsed_NEW_FORMAT.
	• [ ] 1.2 ACTION — IOC pull. Run S2. Work exfil-flagged rows and any __NEEDS_REVIEW__ first. Diff any ?t=//hi/ tenant-string callbacks against real WPaaS identifiers (internal check) — match = possible exfil = CSIRT.
	• [ ] 1.3 ACTION — Infra sweep. Run S4 (now includes Mandiant IPs 143.198.7.94, 157.254.167.12). Classify each hit by direction: inbound = delivery (expected), outbound = execution (escalate).
Phase 2 — Quiet-88772 & webshell hunts (run only if their gate cleared)
	• [ ] 2.1 ACTION (if 0.5 cleared) — DTLS exploit-pattern hunt. Run H5. A SSL_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE / DTLSv1.0 / Internal Error followed within minutes by an NSPPE termination on the same appliance = high-confidence 88772 exploitation. This is the signal H3 could not reach. Escalate any correlated pair.
	• [ ] 2.2 ACTION (if 0.6 cleared) — Webshell interaction hunt. Run S3. 404s with multi-KB bodies / long processing on /vpn/media/*.ico or /vpn/scripts/ = WHIPSHOT-style read-back. Confirm no legit receiver.min.css/.ico ships by that name first.
	• [ ] 2.3 ACTION (if 0.6 cleared) — C2-header hunt. Run H6. Requests carrying HTTP_NSC_LDAP, HTTP_NSC_CLIENTTYPE, or HTTP_X_UX* headers = webshell C2 channel.
Phase 3 — Persistence detection & review sweeps
	• [ ] 3.1 ACTION — New-account detection (Bleed 4). Run Bleed 4 detection-only. Any new system account is alert-worthy (baseline ~zero). Privileged + external = top. Record pitboss_lag_hours on any hit (feeds go-live window tuning).
	• [ ] 3.2 ACTION — First-ever-login sweep (Angle B). Run S-B (review-only). Work REVIEW_HIGH_external_first_login first. Baseline against known accounts before believing any hit.
	• [ ] 3.3 REVIEW — ${jndi vector. 128 events seen in CMD_EXECUTED user field (10/1). Decide: quick standalone check or fold into entropy sweep. Second injection vector, separate from pitboss.
Phase 4 — Operator-side (hand off; cannot run in Splunk)
	• [ ] 4.1 ACTION — Send operator ask (OPERATOR-ASK block below). Bundles all on-box IOCs, Mandiant grep commands, egress target list, DTLS//var/core requests, and session/credential rotation items.
	• [ ] 4.2 ACTION — Provide GTIG YARA (WHIPSHOT, SLAPSHOT, config, C2-header, persistence rules — in YARA block) to whoever can scan the appliance filesystem / EDR. These are file-scan rules, not SPL.
Phase 5 — The open active hunt (the reason the hunt exists)
	• [ ] 5.1 CONFIRM — ICAUUID extraction (H4a Step 0). Run H4a-STEP0. Need clean state, single length, user present. Fix extraction before the main run or replay hides in split groups.
	• [ ] 5.2 ACTION — H4a session replay. Run H4a. Session established through a hit gateway later appearing from a non-WPaaS origin. This is the delivery→session-abuse bridge; Mandiant confirms in-campaign credential/session theft, so treat as live.

