H5 — DTLS Exploit-Pattern → NSPPE Termination (CVE-2026-88772, NEW)
Runnable only if PRE-4 shows SSL/DTLS events. Mandiant: successful 88772 produces a SSL_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE / DTLSv1.0 / Internal Error, and (in /var/log/messages) an NSPPE termination (orphan rings, pitboss … NOT restarting NSPPE). The high-confidence signal is the two correlated within minutes on one appliance.
index=<your_citrix_index> sourcetype="citrix:netscaler:syslog"
    ("SSL_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE" OR "orphan rings" OR "NOT restarting NSPPE")
    earliest="09/01/2026:00:00:00" latest="10/01/2026:23:59:59"
| eval sig=case(
    match(_raw,"SSL_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE") AND match(_raw,"DTLSv1\.0") AND match(_raw,"Internal Error"),"dtls_exploit_pattern",
    match(_raw,"orphan rings") OR match(_raw,"NOT restarting NSPPE"),"nsppe_termination",
    true(),"other")
| where sig!="other"
| bin _time span=5m
| stats values(sig) as signals dc(sig) as sig_types count values(_raw) as samples by host _time
| where sig_types>1 OR match(mvjoin(signals,","),"dtls_exploit_pattern")
| eval severity=if(sig_types>1,"CRITICAL_dtls_plus_nsppe_crash","HIGH_dtls_pattern")
| convert timeformat="%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z" ctime(_time)
| sort - severity _time
Read: CRITICAL = handshake failure + NSPPE termination in the same 5-min bin on one appliance → strong 88772 exploitation. If NSPPE-termination lines are absent (PRE-4), you only have the DTLS half — the termination half is an operator /var/log/messages ask.

